2026-11-19 00:00:51,838 - test - INFO - Existing record: {'id': UUID('01a1ef4e-6c09-795d-89d0-8443ad181a8d'), 'title': 'Tech Stocks Lead Bursa Malaysia Gainers As Nestle, Plantation Heavyweights Drag - BusinessToday', 'link': 'https://businesstoday.com.my/2026/11/18/tech-stocks-lead-bursa-malaysia-gainers-as-nestle-plantation-heavyweights-drag', 'snippet': 'Reach Publishing Sdn Bhd 15-3, Block F1, Jalan PJU 1/42, Dataran Prima, 47301, Petaling Jaya, Selangor\nTechnology and semiconductor-related stocks dominated Bursa Malaysia’s top gainers on Nov 18, led by Malaysian Pacific Industries Bhd (MPI), while Nestle (M) Bhd and plantation heavyweights topped the losers’ list despite positive broader market sentiment.', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 11, 18, 9, 37, 36, 426015, tzinfo=zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(key='Etc/UTC')), 'source': 'businesstoday.com.my', 'article_language': None, 'article_type': 'news', 'content': 'Technology and semiconductor-related stocks dominated Bursa Malaysia’s top gainers on Nov 18, led by Malaysian Pacific Industries Bhd (MPI), while Nestle (M) Bhd and plantation heavyweights topped the losers’ list despite positive broader market sentiment.\nMPI emerged as the biggest gainer, jumping 70 sen to RM36.40, followed by Kelington Group Bhd and Mi Technovation Bhd, which both climbed 34 sen to RM7.14 and RM5.78, respectively.\nUWC Bhd advanced 28 sen to RM5.86, while TMK Chemical Bhd gained 21 sen to RM3.11, rounding out the top five gainers.\nOn the losing front, Nestle suffered the steepest decline, shedding 96 sen to RM94.30, followed by Kuala Lumpur Kepong Bhd, which fell 32 sen to RM20.80.\nPress Metal Aluminium Holdings Bhd dropped 21 sen to RM6.65, while Batu Kawan Bhd and Carlsberg Brewery Malaysia Bhd each declined 18 sen to RM19 and RM12.70, respectively.\nDespite the mixed performance among heavyweights, market breadth remained positive, with 630 gainers outnumbering 430 losers. Another 476 counters were unchanged, 1,247 untraded and 14 suspended.\nTotal trading volume eased to 3.06 billion units from Nov 17’s 3.35 billion units, although transaction value rose to RM2.76 billion from RM2.28 billion, indicating stronger trading value despite lower overall volume.', 'content_status': 'completed', 'content_error': None, 'embedding': '[-0.052686132,-0.0053855404,-0.016359422,-0.0066639953,-0.0040758206,-0.027493125,-0.0054414226,0.010782472,0.015711548,0.033796318,-0.039763696,0.0056506884,-0.0034375498,-0.004222855,-0.008633439,-0.030079782,0.0579861,-0.0020794077,-0.003897084,-0.0187508,0.0020922353,0.04887366,0.0027165937,0.021084253,0.015661743,0.035916086,0.0060389815,-0.0083060125,0.030635118,0.04254624,-0.0021632481,-0.0097266985,0.023967484,0.006954677,-0.027196992,-0.0050289147,0.025588127,-0.06511912,-0.02468957,-0.021547683,0.02543082,0.03788866,-0.026651857,0.019352838,0.07814727,-0.0013352868,-0.028812371,-0.0030430749,-0.031044329,0.020972721,0.056696773,-0.043719623,0.043916013,-0.03104522,0.05885837,-0.02807868,-0.034708977,-0.021934133,-0.050244417,0.0033189869,-0.014708456,0.030783886,0.027516793,-0.01934908,0.004790415,0.08729636,0.008913813,-6.2399005e-05,-0.030909592,-0.025298825,-0.0395192,0.0074837087,0.06366648,-0.033217873,-0.071343616,-0.018277166,0.024264228,0.017590085,0.031127587,-0.027867118,0.024737353,-0.011205229,-0.015196134,-0.0058258967,0.009409616,0.027635768,-0.019315002,-0.007700986,-0.0045868503,-0.0028603582,0.02713304,-0.031553403,-0.019887827,-0.029484073,-0.003587967,0.0060292254,-0.04007931,0.023973469,-0.010633443,-0.0050156694,-0.005434638,-0.011016564,0.06396229,0.0054013496,0.0145379435,-0.033460665,0.0071049184,0.02194613,-0.0027962802,-0.03883313,0.010486737,-0.029836938,0.031040302,-0.018328892,-0.0018952342,-0.03900074,0.024706708,0.023302345,0.08222845,0.019526515,0.016683627,0.031894177,0.06097604,-0.033119176,-0.023475079,-0.050929416,0.014561124,0.0042186803,-0.007456805,0.01828421,0.010910041,-0.023612432,-0.056069184,0.018541478,-0.03446321,-0