2026-11-19 11:18:23,521 - test - INFO - Existing record: {'id': UUID('01a1f1cd-b80e-7e92-9171-cb1541e4c6c9'), 'title': 'Take-Two Shares Surge Over 8% As GTA VI Reviews Fuel Sales Optimism', 'link': 'https://businesstoday.com.my/2026/11/19/take-two-shares-surge-over-8-as-gta-vi-reviews-fuel-sales-optimism', 'snippet': 'Reach Publishing Sdn Bhd 15-3, Block F1, Jalan PJU 1/42, Dataran Prima, 47301, Petaling Jaya, Selangor\nShares of Take-Two Interactive surged more than 8% on Wednesday as positive early reviews of "Grand Theft Auto VI" boosted investor confidence in the blockbuster game\'s sales potential and the publisher\'s revenue outlook.', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 11, 19, 1, 15, 52, 498289, tzinfo=zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(key='Etc/UTC')), 'source': 'businesstoday.com.my', 'article_language': None, 'article_type': 'news', 'content': 'Shares of Take-Two Interactive surged more than 8% on Wednesday as positive early reviews of “Grand Theft Auto VI” boosted investor confidence in the blockbuster game’s sales potential and the publisher’s revenue outlook.\nThe stock was the top gainer on the Nasdaq-100 index, recovering from a 19% decline year-to-date through Tuesday’s close, as players and critics gave the latest instalment in the franchise an early score of 99 on review aggregator Metacritic.\nThe game, which follows more than 13 years after its predecessor, has generated intense anticipation, with some players reportedly taking several days of leave and making arrangements with partners to secure uninterrupted gaming time.\nNick McKay, senior analyst for video gaming and digital entertainment at Freedom Capital Markets, said the strong Metacritic score had addressed concerns over whether the game could meet expectations.\n“The wait appears to have been worth it for gamers and investors alike,” he said.\nAnalysts at Wells Fargo raised their estimates for GTA VI sales to about 65 million units in Take-Two’s current financial year ending March, up from their previous projection of 35 million units.\nThe revised forecast also factors in the possibility of a PC release in early 2027.\nReuters\nThe brokerage lifted its annual bookings forecast for Take-Two by 19% to US$9.76 billion, above the LSEG consensus estimate of US$8 billion and the company’s own guidance of between US$8 billion and US$8.20 billion.\nOppenheimer separately estimated that GTA VI could generate about US$1.85 billion in gross revenue during its first three days, compared with the US$1 billion recorded by predecessor GTA V following its 2013 release.\nThe game’s launch is also expected to benefit the wider gaming industry, with research firm Newzoo forecasting 3% growth in the global console player base in 2026, compared with a likely decline without the release.\n“Few releases can change how the whole console market spends, and GTA VI is one of those rare titles,” said Emmanuel Rosier, Newzoo’s director of market intelligence.\nBeyond gaming, the launch could also drive activity across other digital platforms and consumer services.\nAnalytics firm Sensor Tower estimated that the release could generate more than 50 million additional visits to food delivery and restaurant applications in the United States within 30 days, as players spend extended periods gaming.\nSocial media platforms such as YouTube and Reddit are also expected to see increased engagement as fans discuss the game and share gameplay clips.\nShares of DoorDash rose 2%, while Reddit edged marginally higher.\nAs of noon Eastern Time on Wednesday, about 17.1 million units of GTA VI had been sold, according to a Sensor Tower tracker, exceeding pre-order volumes for major game releases in recent history.', 'content_status': 'completed', 'content_error': None, 'embedding': '[-0.0063568195,-0.029172719,-0.018298855,0.037435915,0.019510701,-0.009101537,0.011934154,0.004868736,0.010456983,0.002101325,0.0063518495,-0.008805674,-0.025393778,-0.02463923,-0.04465136,-0.014357632,0.003522933,-0.0078383