2026-11-19 11:21:24,965 - test - INFO - Existing record: {'id': UUID('01a1f1cd-b795-7a11-8c1f-f8c38dfc8257'), 'title': 'Umno to lose S’gor constituency coordinators after Bersatu CSA | FMT', 'link': 'https://www.freemalaysiatoday.com/category/nation/2026/11/19/umno-to-lose-s-gor-constituency-coordinators-after-bersatu-csa', 'snippet': "The 56-member Selangor assembly comprises 32 assemblymen from PH, 11 from Bersatu, 10 from PAS, two from Umno and one independent. (Facebook pic) PETALING JAYA: Umno is set to lose its constituency coordinator positions in several seats in Selangor after Bersatu signs a confidence and supply ...\nThe 56-member Selangor assembly comprises 32 assemblymen from PH, 11 from Bersatu, 10 from PAS, two from Umno and one independent. (Facebook pic) PETALING JAYA: Umno is set to lose its constituency coordinator positions in several seats in Selangor after Bersatu signs a confidence and supply agreement (CSA) with menteri besar Amirudin Shari’s administration, says a source.\nBersatu source says the position of Umno's Rizam Ismail in the state exco will also be discussed by the state government after the CSA is signed.\nThis is because opposition assemblymen in Selangor are not given access to constituency development funds from the state government.\nLast month, Amirudin said Bersatu assemblymen in Selangor would sign a CSA with his administration before the state budget is tabled, with the terms being finalised.", 'published_at': None, 'source': 'www.freemalaysiatoday.com', 'article_language': None, 'article_type': 'news', 'content': 'The source from Bersatu said the CSA was already in the final stage, with the Perikatan Nasional (PN) component’s assemblymen to remain on the opposition bench in the state assembly while obtaining “backbencher status”.\nThe source said Bersatu assemblymen would then be roped into state executive council committees, district offices and local councils.\n“All of Umno’s constituency coordinators in Bersatu seats will be terminated since they will no longer be required.\n“Meanwhile, Umno constituency coordinators in PAS seats will be replaced with coordinators from Bersatu,” the source told FMT.\nThe source said the position of Umno assemblyman Rizam Ismail in the state exco would be discussed by the administration after the CSA is signed.\nFMT has reached out to Amirudin’s office for comment.\nConstituency coordinators are only appointed in opposition-held seats to coordinate and manage the state government’s development funds in these areas.\nThis is because opposition assemblymen in Selangor are not given access to constituency development funds from the state government.\nThis development comes amid worsening ties between Pakatan Harapan (PH) and Barisan Nasional, especially after the latter formed alliances with PN in the Negeri Sembilan and Melaka elections.\nWhile Bersatu is a PN component, it appears to be on the verge of leaving the coalition it founded following a fallout with PAS, which chairs PN.\nLast month, Amirudin said Bersatu assemblymen in Selangor would sign a CSA with his administration before the state budget is tabled, with the terms being finalised.\nSix Bersatu MPs have similarly signed a CSA with the PH-led federal government, granting them access to constituency development funds.\nThe 56-member Selangor assembly comprises 32 assemblymen from PH, 11 from Bersatu, 10 from PAS, two from Umno and one independent. However, not all of Bersatu’s assemblymen are aligned with the current leadership.', 'content_status': 'completed', 'content_error': None, 'embedding': '[-0.013285988,-0.0004995636,-0.051794775,0.0004960748,0.025083711,-0.044975456,0.038527094,-0.03534618,0.05090303,0.03215475,0.034674916,0.025239298,0.020369422,0.03867207,-0.04267118,-0.018700544,0.059089188,-0.010428355,0.013702189,0.00659761,0.02265454,-0.01928295,-0.00032467832,0.0065985546,0.030947236,0.024341762,-0.018542353,0.03005946,-0.0002692333,0.028483186,-0.002949747,-0.021889428,0