2026-11-19 11:35:33,199 - test - INFO - Existing record: {'id': UUID('01a1f1cd-b64a-79f5-97ad-a8500f6ed337'), 'title': 'Big Caring Group Makes Tepid Bursa Debut, Opens 2.78% Below IPO Price', 'link': 'https://businesstoday.com.my/2026/11/19/big-caring-group-makes-tepid-bursa-debut-opens-2-78-below-ipo-price', 'snippet': 'Reach Publishing Sdn Bhd 15-3, Block F1, Jalan PJU 1/42, Dataran Prima, 47301, Petaling Jaya, Selangor\nBig Caring Group Bhd opened at RM1.05 on its Main Market debut, 3 sen or 2.78% below its IPO price of RM1.08, despite strong demand from retail investors ahead of its listing.', 'published_at': datetime.datetime(2026, 11, 19, 1, 15, 52, 497129, tzinfo=zoneinfo.ZoneInfo(key='Etc/UTC')), 'source': 'businesstoday.com.my', 'article_language': None, 'article_type': 'news', 'content': 'Big Caring Group Bhd opened at RM1.05 on its Main Market debut, 3 sen or 2.78% below its IPO price of RM1.08, despite strong demand from retail investors ahead of its listing.\nThe pharmacy group’s shares subsequently fell to RM0.995 as at 9.01am, down 8.5 sen or 7.87% from its IPO price, after trading between RM0.99 and RM1.06.\nTrading volume stood at 23.53 million shares.\nThe debut follows an encouraging response to its IPO, which was oversubscribed by 4.31 times, attracting 29,474 applications for 783.75 million shares from the Malaysian public.\nIn an exclusive interview with BusinessToday ahead of the listing, group managing director and chief executive officer Lee Meng Chuan described the IPO as a natural progression for the business after two decades of expansion.\nThe group is allocating RM570.7 million, or 89.5% of its public issue proceeds, towards partially repaying bank borrowings. The repayment is expected to reduce its gearing from 2.8 times to 0.9 times and generate annual interest savings of approximately RM26.3 million.\nBig Caring also plans to open between 40 and 50 new retail pharmacy outlets annually over the next three to five years, supported by annual capital expenditure of approximately RM18 million.\nThe group reported a net profit attributable to shareholders of RM72.5 million on revenue of RM1.11 billion for its first quarter ended Sept 30, 2026. Its retail segment contributed RM1.04 billion, or 93.3% of total revenue.\nLee said the group would focus on delivering its growth plans following the listing, with strategic acquisitions and organic expansion remaining its two key growth engines.', 'content_status': 'completed', 'content_error': None, 'embedding': '[-0.058272894,-0.021815171,-0.025819661,-0.00069046067,0.0056247106,-0.012395202,-0.00013269311,-0.03344517,-0.023305956,0.027457023,0.0074274563,0.008723652,-0.020536803,-0.0061996183,-0.040056225,0.020009387,0.053580567,-0.003851567,-0.026246633,-0.015641538,-0.025537802,0.07009602,0.039153393,0.008017992,-0.037348785,0.024337681,-0.038401704,-0.013013952,0.031026525,0.027824162,0.007702629,-0.014928699,0.05842067,0.0068992195,0.031063305,-0.013929996,0.0069809044,-0.03994863,-0.014694856,0.01780938,0.033342876,0.03408505,0.011309049,0.046932567,0.035739824,-0.03690222,-0.024747966,0.0074290973,-0.008076611,-0.0041337516,0.045578036,-0.03539917,-0.039480567,-0.037509292,0.0063000307,-0.007140458,-0.0032834443,-0.021050438,0.0052760085,-0.0051709884,-0.045536496,0.028615665,0.010257879,-0.023952743,-0.0050528687,0.050427925,0.005774595,-0.0110646915,-0.012832239,-0.040065315,-0.010638829,0.0392353,0.07710689,-0.0075347796,-0.042747468,0.009824407,-0.009652989,0.00543908,-0.009616851,-0.04899175,0.005567433,0.022747047,-0.06638794,-0.0010319188,-0.0068218512,0.03921237,-0.03317525,0.04090337,-0.019757735,0.048970383,-0.022284903,-0.03820669,0.00016401798,0.0022268705,-0.017499313,0.006134267,-0.047447544,0.050697885,0.0028052926,0.029755995,-0.016974851,0.00045722813,0.0006020536,0.007394221,0.015008124,-0.01231871,0.00019054179,0.039058242,-0.038814656,-0.025024677,0.0007235043,0.00859342,0.008023492,0.008616772,-0.017663822,-0.001013869,0.01797793